(footprint "LitzPad_15A"
  (version 20240108)
  (generator "hand-built")
  (descr "High-current litz wire termination pad, 15A rated. 8.0 mm dia pad, 3.0 mm dia hole. Dimension sourcing: generic high-current PTH pad spec; low confidence — no part-specific datasheet exists for this custom coil terminal. Flagged for human visual cross-check before fabrication. PITCH CORRECTED 2026-07-29 (docs/brainstorms/2026-07-29-hv-footprint-copper-shorts-requirements.md Case 2): this is R30, Sheetpath tank.inductor_conn -- the two ends of the resonant tank coil itself (pad 1 net tank.c_tank1-p2, pad 2 net tank-out; elec/src/modules.ato). The prior 5.0mm pitch on 8.0mm pads gave -3.0mm (3.0mm of copper OVERLAP), a fabrication-blocking short between the tank's two highest-differential-voltage nodes, unconditionally wrong regardless of the voltage question below. New pitch 13.0mm = 8.0mm pad dia + 5.0mm creepage, where 5.0mm is docs/specs/HIGH_VOLTAGE_CLEARANCE_SPEC.md Sec 5.1's IEC 60335-1 Table 16 (Pollution Degree 2, Material Group IIIb) BASIC-insulation creepage figure at 400V -- the applicable category since both pads are the same tank circuit (not a mains/SELV boundary; c.f. scripts/generate_kicad_dru.py's separately-lower 'HV internal same footprint' 1.5mm, which is a TO-247-pin-pitch compromise for a manufacturer-fixed package and does not apply here since this footprint's geometry is fully our own choice). 400V is elec/src/modules.ato's declared v_tank_peak (asserted design floor, used elsewhere for c_tank1/c_tank2 voltage-rating margin). NOT FULLY RESOLVED, flagged for human sign-off before fabrication: (1) docs/evidence/2026-07-27-inductance-range-sweep.md reports simulated peak tank-cap voltage up to 867V across the L range the repo still considers plausible (coil L is an unresolved assumption per docs/hardware/TANK_COIL_SPECIFICATION.md, 'L cannot be specified from the current model') -- if the finalized L pushes working voltage above 400V, this 13.0mm/5.0mm figure is a floor, not sufficient, and must be re-derived at the higher voltage (HIGH_VOLTAGE_CLEARANCE_SPEC.md's own table stops at 400V for creepage / 600V for clearance, so a >400V case needs a fresh standard lookup, not extrapolation from this table). (2) The 8.0mm pad diameter itself is unchanged and remains the original 'generic ... low confidence, no part-specific datasheet' figure -- widening only the pitch does not source the diameter; confirm the actual lug/terminal size against a real 15A litz-wire termination spec before fabrication.")
  (tags "litz custom coil terminal high_current")
  (attr through_hole)
  (pad "1" thru_hole circle (at 0 0) (size 8.0 8.0) (drill 3.0) (layers "*.Cu" "*.Mask"))
  (pad "2" thru_hole circle (at 13.0 0) (size 8.0 8.0) (drill 3.0) (layers "*.Cu" "*.Mask"))
)
